The Mercedes-Benz A170 CDI was part of the W169 generation (2004-2012). Based on the search results, the A170 CDI typically had a 1.7L diesel engine producing 116 hp and 250 Nm (184 lb-ft) of torque. It was available with a 5-speed manual or a CVT (Autotronic) transmission. 0-60 mph acceleration is estimated around 10.8-11.0 seconds, and top speed is around 118 mph (190 km/h). Fuel economy is quite good for its time, around 47-50 mpg US combined (5.0-5.3 L/100km). CO2 emissions are around 132-140 g/km. The car's dimensions are around 3838 mm length, 1764 mm width, and 1593 mm height, with a wheelbase of 2568 mm. Cargo space is around 435-1370 L (15.4-48.4 cu ft). It has 5 seats and is FWD. Turning circle is around 10.9-11 meters (35.9-36.09 ft). The W169 received a 5-star Euro NCAP safety rating. Insurance groups for the W169 A-Class range from 5 to 16, with the A170 CDI likely in the mid-range. Used prices in the UK are typically low, reflecting its age. Reliability concerns include potential issues with the CVT transmission, fuel injection, and rust. Ground clearance is listed as 11.3-12.4 cm (4.45-4.9 inches).

